---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { ArrowUpRight, ArrowRight } from '@lucide/astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const sources = [
['serhii-londar/open-source-mac-os-apps','https://github.com/serhii-londar/open-source-mac-os-apps'],
['jaywcjlove/awesome-mac','https://github.com/jaywcjlove/awesome-mac'],
['jeffreyjackson/mac-apps','https://github.com/jeffreyjackson/mac-apps'],
['iCHAIT/awesome-macOS','https://github.com/iCHAIT/awesome-macOS'],
['abordage/awesome-mac','https://github.com/abordage/awesome-mac'],
['AndrewSB/awesome-macOS','https://github.com/AndrewSB/awesome-macOS'],
['Awesome-llms-labs/awesome-oss-macos','https://github.com/Awesome-llms-labs/awesome-oss-macos']
];
---
<Layout title="The idea — OpenStore" active="about">
  <article class="about-page"><h1>Your Mac deserves<br/>a little more open.</h1><p class="about-lead">Great software is being made in the open, every day. OpenStore is a place to find it, understand it, and support the people behind it.</p><a class="button button-dark" href={`${base}#catalog`}>Explore the collection <ArrowRight size={16}/></a>
    <section><h2>A collection with a point of view.</h2><p>We’re building a useful starting point for open-source software on macOS. Small menu bar helpers sit alongside creative tools, text editors, and everyday essentials. Each listing brings together what matters: what it does, what it looks like, its source code, and its license.</p><p>OpenStore is a community project by <a href="https://github.com/koative">Koative</a>. It’s an independent directory, not an app installer or a software marketplace. Official project pages handle downloads, support, and any paid distribution options.</p></section>
    <div class="about-principles"><article><h3>Open means open source.</h3><p>Free to download is not the same as open source. We check each project’s source license and exclude licenses with additional use restrictions.</p></article><article><h3>Evidence, not guesswork.</h3><p>Every entry links to the repository and license we checked, with a verification date. That date is a record of our review, not a security certification.</p></article><article><h3>Real apps. Real images.</h3><p>Icons and screenshots come from the original projects. Their sources, credits, and rights travel with each listing. No generated app screenshots.</p></article><article><h3>One folder. One contribution.</h3><p>A small Markdown file and its images power the website and README together. Everything is versioned, reviewable, and easy to improve.</p></article></div>
    <section><h2>Standing on open shoulders.</h2><p>This collection started with Jeffrey Jackson’s Mac apps list and grew through research across these community directories. They’re discovery sources; each application is verified independently.</p><ul class="source-list">{sources.map(([name,url]) => <li><a href={url}>{name}<ArrowUpRight size={16}/></a></li>)}</ul><p>Read our <a href="https://github.com/koative/openstore/blob/main/docs/RESEARCH.md">research and inclusion policy</a> for the comparisons, exclusions, and licensing details.</p></section>
    <section><h2>There’s room on the shelf.</h2><p>Have an app we should know about? Found an outdated link or a better screenshot? You don’t need to be the original developer to help.</p><a class="button button-dark" href="https://github.com/koative/openstore/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">Contribute to OpenStore <ArrowUpRight size={16}/></a></section>
  </article>
</Layout>
